{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"Under Regulation 26(2), dealing arrangements must generally be consistent across share classes. The Central Bank’s 2026 guidance expressly permits different cut-offs for **cash versus in-kind** subscriptions/redemptions, and for **currency-hedged versus unhedged classes**, where the operational differences justify them and the arrangements are properly disclosed.\n\nThat is distinct from the older **Q&A 1030** approach: it treated differing cut-offs between share classes as a departure from the rule requiring a common dealing cut-off, requiring a **Central Bank waiver**. The Q&A waiver route is not the basis for the specific exceptions expressly recognized in 2026; nor should those exceptions be read as a general permission for any class-level cut-off variation."}}
